        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I don't think inlining `libiconv` is feasible -- it's just too large, and not even built on all platforms (macOS ignores the bundled `libiconv` and `gettext`). \n\nFor `gettext`, we need to distinguish the `libintl.h` header (which Neovim itself needs) and the CLI tools (`msgmerge`, `msgfmt`, `xgettext`), which are only used during the build process. So it might be feasible to\n1. inline https://github.com/sabotage-linux/gettext-tiny/blob/master/include/libintl.h into our `gettext_defs.h`\n2. make GNU `gettext` (installed via, e.g., homebrew or VCPKG if necessary) a hard build dependency.\n",
            "created_at": "2026-08-29T11:42:03Z",
